 E(8,'Jane Is Publicly Cleared','After Mr Lloyd confirms the account, Miss Temple announces that Jane is innocent.','schoolroom',S(['jane','Returns to study with reputation restored and energy released from defensive shame.'],['temple','Uses evidence and authority to repair a public wrong.']),day(1801,2,20,9),3,{threads:['education','equality'],motifs:['documents','voices']}),
 E(9,'Typhus Exposes Lowood','Disease spreads through the underfed school, drawing outside attention to its conditions.','lowood-yard',S(['jane','Moves among the healthier pupils with new freedom while recognizing the cost of neglect.'],['temple','Nurses and organizes beyond the capacity of the institution’s poor provisions.'],['brocklehurst','Loses unquestioned control as deaths make his economy visible to the public.']),day(1801,5,10,12),5,{threads:['education','class-work'],motifs:['food','weather']}),
 E(9,'Jane Lies Beside Helen','Jane finds Helen dying of consumption and spends the night beside her.','dormitory',S(['jane','Seeks closeness against rules and holds Helen while facing death without adult mediation.'],['helen','Meets death with the same spiritual confidence she tried to teach Jane.']),day(1801,6,5,23),5,{threads:['faith','belonging'],motifs:['rooms','voices']}),
 E(10,'Eight Years at Lowood Pass','Reform improves the school; Jane becomes first a successful pupil and then a teacher.','schoolroom',S(['jane','Builds discipline, knowledge, and competence within the institution that once shamed her.'],['temple','Provides the stable example under which Jane’s intellectual life develops.']),day(1809,6,1,10),2,{threads:['education','freedom'],motifs:['books']}),
 E(10,'Jane Advertises for Change','Miss Temple’s marriage and departure awaken Jane’s desire for a wider field, so she seeks a governess post.','lowood-gate',S(['jane','Turns restlessness into a practical advertisement and accepts responsibility for leaving safely.']),day(1809,8,10,15),2,{items:['advertisement'],threads:['education','freedom'],motifs:['documents','thresholds']}),
 E(11,'Jane Arrives at Thornfield','Mrs Fairfax welcomes Jane, and Adèle’s presence clarifies the work awaiting her.','thornfield-gate',S(['jane','Reaches the new estate relieved by warmth but uncertain about the household’s structure.'],['fairfax','Receives the governess as a companion as well as an employee.'],['adele','Meets her new teacher with quick curiosity and rehearsed social charm.']),day(1809,10,15,20),2,{threads:['class-work','belonging'],motifs:['thresholds','fire-ice']}),
 E(11,'A Strange Laugh Crosses the Passage','During a tour of Thornfield, an uncanny laugh is attributed to Grace Poole.','third-floor',S(['jane','Registers the sound as inconsistent with the quiet domestic explanation offered below.'],['fairfax','Identifies Grace without revealing the guarded arrangement of the upper floor.'],['grace','Remains associated with work whose purpose Jane is not invited to question.']),day(1809,10,16,11),3,{items:['third-floor-key'],threads:['secret'],motifs:['voices','rooms']}),
 E(12,'Jane Leaves the House for Hay','Jane passes through the garden side of Thornfield on an errand that answers her need for movement beyond the household.','garden-door',S(['jane','Crosses from the governed interior into winter air with the temporary freedom of a solitary walk.']),day(1810,1,12,15),2,{threads:['freedom','class-work'],motifs:['thresholds','weather']}),
 E(12,'Jane Walks Toward Hay','Routine and confinement make Jane seek air, distance, and an errand beyond the estate.','hay-lane',S(['jane','Moves independently through the winter evening, resisting the idea that safety should mean stagnation.']),day(1810,1,12,16),2,{threads:['freedom','class-work'],motifs:['weather','thresholds']}),
 E(12,'Jane Helps a Fallen Rider','A horse slips on ice; Jane assists the injured stranger who will prove to be Rochester.','hay-lane',S(['jane','Responds practically to danger and speaks without the self-consciousness his rank will later impose.'],['rochester','Accepts help from an unknown young woman while testing her account of where she lives.']),day(1810,1,12,17),4,{threads:['love-equality'],motifs:['weather','thresholds']}),
 E(13,'Rochester Questions the Governess','Back at Thornfield, Rochester asks about Jane’s history, education, and accomplishments.','schoolroom-thornfield',S(['jane','Answers with precision and refuses to perform exaggerated gratitude or inferiority.'],['rochester','Finds her directness more engaging than conventional deference.'],['adele','Displays the accomplishments she believes will earn her guardian’s approval.']),day(1810,1,13,19),3,{threads:['love-equality','class-work'],motifs:['voices','watching']}),
 E(13,'Jane’s Drawings Are Examined','Rochester studies three watercolours and recognizes emotional experience beyond Jane’s formal biography.','schoolroom-thornfield',S(['jane','Allows her private imagination to be judged without apologizing for its ambition.'],['rochester','Reads the portfolio as evidence of solitude, discipline, and a mind he wants to question further.']),day(1810,1,13,20),3,{items:['drawings'],threads:['love-equality'],motifs:['portraits','visions']}),
 E(14,'Jane Refuses Flattery and Submission','Rochester presses Jane into an intense fireside conversation about command, experience, and remorse.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Maintains moral and intellectual independence even while fascinated by her employer.'],['rochester','Tests whether authority, confession, and charm can make Jane speak on equal terms.']),day(1810,1,20,20),3,{threads:['love-equality','equality'],motifs:['fire-ice','voices']}),
 E(14,'Rochester Hints at Reformation','He speaks of past error and a hoped-for new life without naming the obstacle hidden in the house.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Offers judgment without pretending to absolve conduct she does not know.'],['rochester','Begins imagining Jane as the means of renewal while withholding the fact that limits his choices.']),day(1810,1,20,21),3,{threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['voices']}),
 E(15,'Rochester Explains Adèle’s Place','Rochester recounts Céline Varens’s betrayal and why he brought Adèle to England.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Separates Adèle’s need for care from the vanity of the adults in her origin story.'],['rochester','Frames guardianship as reluctant duty while revealing an older wound to pride.'],['adele','Remains the child whose security depends on decisions made around her.']),day(1810,1,27,20),2,{threads:['belonging','love-equality'],motifs:['voices']}),
 E(15,'Jane Saves Rochester from Fire','Smoke wakes Jane; she finds Rochester’s curtains burning and extinguishes the flames.','rochester-room',S(['jane','Acts immediately, then demands an explanation for a danger too deliberate to dismiss.'],['rochester','Entrusts Jane with silence, checks the upper floor, and returns emotionally shaken by her rescue.'],['grace','Is named as the culprit while the actual source remains confined above.']),day(1810,1,28,2),5,{threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['fire-ice','rooms']}),
 E(16,'Grace Poole Remains at Thornfield','The morning after the fire, Jane finds Grace sewing calmly and apparently unpunished.','third-floor',S(['jane','Questions the official explanation because Grace’s security contradicts the alleged crime.'],['grace','Maintains professional composure and warns Jane indirectly against curiosity.']),day(1810,1,28,10),3,{threads:['secret'],motifs:['watching','rooms']}),
 E(16,'Jane Draws Two Portraits','Learning that Blanche Ingram may marry Rochester, Jane contrasts her own plain image with an imagined society beauty.','schoolroom-thornfield',S(['jane','Uses drawing to discipline hope and confront the economic distance between herself and Rochester.'],['blanche','Exists for Jane first as a socially perfected rival constructed from description.']),day(1810,2,1,19),3,{items:['drawings'],threads:['love-equality','class-work'],motifs:['portraits']}),
 E(17,'The Ingram Party Arrives','Rochester returns with fashionable guests who fill Thornfield with display and hierarchy.','thornfield-hall',S(['jane','Watches from the edge of the household, professionally required to attend yet socially excluded.'],['rochester','Stages a brilliant house party while monitoring Jane’s response.'],['blanche','Takes the most visible place among the guests and treats governesses as socially negligible.'],['adele','Delights in costumes, music, and the promise of adult attention.']),day(1810,3,10,18),3,{threads:['love-equality','class-work'],motifs:['watching','thresholds']}),
 E(17,'Jane Observes Blanche and Rochester','Music and conversation make the apparent courtship public while Jane measures affection against performance.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Accepts her love privately without mistaking spectacle for mutual understanding.'],['rochester','Keeps Blanche’s attention while repeatedly checking whether Jane is watching.'],['blanche','Performs wit and accomplishment for a marriage she understands as a social triumph.']),day(1810,3,10,21),3,{threads:['love-equality','class-work'],motifs:['watching','voices']}),
 E(18,'The Guests Perform Charades','Rochester and Blanche enact courtship, marriage, and captivity before the assembled company.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Reads the tableaux closely and sees display where others assume intimacy.'],['rochester','Uses theatrical roles to cultivate the appearance of an approaching match.'],['blanche','Enjoys occupying the visible position of bride and chosen partner.']),day(1810,3,12,20),3,{threads:['love-equality','secret'],motifs:['confinement','watching']}),
 E(18,'A Gypsy Is Announced','A supposed fortune-teller refuses to leave until the unmarried women hear their futures.','thornfield-hall',S(['jane','Approaches the performance skeptically but agrees to a private interview.'],['rochester','Uses disguise to question guests without the constraints of his own identity.']),day(1810,3,13,18),3,{threads:['love-equality','secret'],motifs:['visions','watching']}),
 E(19,'The Gypsy Reads Jane','The disguised Rochester probes Jane’s feelings and claims her face reveals more than her words.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Resists suggestion, then recognizes familiar speech beneath the costume.'],['rochester','Risks manipulation to learn whether Jane’s composure conceals love.']),day(1810,3,13,20),4,{threads:['love-equality','secret'],motifs:['portraits','watching']}),
 E(19,'Richard Mason Arrives','A visitor from Spanish Town abruptly changes Rochester’s confidence.','thornfield-hall',S(['rochester','Reacts to Mason’s name as the return of a history he has kept outside the house’s public life.'],['mason','Enters Thornfield expecting a private meeting with his brother-in-law.'],['jane','Sees Rochester’s strength falter before being asked for reassurance without explanation.']),day(1810,3,13,22),4,{threads:['secret'],motifs:['thresholds','voices']}),
 E(20,'Mason Is Attacked Upstairs','A cry wakes the house; Rochester contains the guests and leads Jane to a bleeding Mason.','third-floor',S(['jane','Obeys a demand for silence while recognizing that the hidden danger is human and violent.'],['rochester','Controls access to the upper floor and tries to remove Mason before the household understands.'],['mason','Endures severe wounds and terror while promising not to speak to his attacker.'],['bertha','Breaks through confinement long enough to wound the brother who entered her room.']),day(1810,3,14,2),5,{items:['third-floor-key'],threads:['secret'],motifs:['rooms','voices']}),
 E(20,'Jane Keeps Watch Beside Mason','Jane sponges blood and prevents conversation until a surgeon can take Mason away.','attic',S(['jane','Provides care while refusing to let fear erase her observation of the locked arrangement.'],['mason','Submits to secrecy and departure despite the seriousness of his injuries.'],['rochester','Relies on Jane’s steadiness while preserving the concealment.']),day(1810,3,14,3),5,{threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['confinement','watching']}),
 E(21,'Jane Returns to Gateshead','Bessie summons Jane to Mrs Reed, whose son is dead and whose health is failing.','gateshead-gate',S(['jane','Returns by choice, prepared to offer care without pretending the childhood injury vanished.'],['bessie','Receives Jane as an accomplished adult rather than the dependent child who left.'],['mrs-reed','Faces illness and family ruin while remaining emotionally fixed against Jane.']),day(1810,4,2,18),3,{threads:['belonging','forgiveness'],motifs:['thresholds']}),
 E(21,'Mrs Reed Reveals John Eyre’s Letter','The dying woman admits that Jane’s uncle sought to adopt her and that she falsely reported Jane dead.','sickroom',S(['jane','Offers reconciliation and receives documentary proof of a lost family possibility.'],['mrs-reed','Confesses concealment without finding the affection Jane still offers.']),day(1810,4,8,16),4,{items:['john-letter'],mentioned:['john-reed'],threads:['belonging','inheritance','forgiveness'],motifs:['documents','voices']}),
 E(22,'Jane Returns to Thornfield','Rochester waits on the road and turns Jane’s homecoming into an intimate welcome.','thornfield-gate',S(['jane','Names Thornfield as home because Rochester’s presence, not property, gives it emotional meaning.'],['rochester','Receives her return with relief while continuing the false Ingram expectation.']),day(1810,5,20,18),3,{threads:['love-equality','belonging'],motifs:['thresholds']}),
 E(22,'Summer Restores Their Familiarity','Jane resumes teaching and evening conversation under the apparent deadline of Rochester’s marriage.','orchard',S(['jane','Lives intensely in the present while preparing herself to lose Thornfield.'],['rochester','Draws Jane closer while allowing her to believe separation is inevitable.'],['adele','Returns to lessons without understanding the threatened change in her household.']),day(1810,6,10,16),2,{threads:['love-equality','class-work'],motifs:['weather','birds']}),
 E(23,'Rochester Announces Jane Must Leave','Under the chestnut tree, Rochester says marriage will send Jane to a distant post.','orchard',S(['jane','Rejects the assumption that poverty and obscurity make her without feeling or spiritual equality.'],['rochester','Pushes the invented separation until Jane finally speaks her love and anger.']),day(1810,6,15,21),5,{threads:['love-equality','equality'],motifs:['voices','birds']}),
 E(23,'Jane Accepts Rochester’s Proposal','Rochester reveals that Blanche was a provocation and asks Jane to marry him; a storm splits the tree that night.','orchard',S(['jane','Accepts only after testing the sincerity of a proposal that seems to overturn every social expectation.'],['rochester','Claims a future with Jane while still concealing the existing marriage that makes the promise impossible.']),day(1810,6,15,22),5,{threads:['love-equality','secret'],motifs:['weather','fire-ice']}),
 E(24,'Jane Resists Being Remade','Rochester orders jewels and luxurious clothes; Jane insists on remaining recognizable to herself.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Refuses ornaments that would turn love into ownership or disguise her working identity.'],['rochester','Expresses delight through possession and display, underestimating how strongly Jane fears dependence.']),day(1810,6,16,14),3,{items:['jewels'],threads:['love-equality','equality'],motifs:['portraits']}),
 E(24,'Jane Seeks Practical Independence','Jane plans to write to her uncle so that any inheritance might lessen the financial imbalance of marriage.','schoolroom-thornfield',S(['jane','Looks for material independence as protection for emotional equality.']),day(1810,6,20,10),2,{items:['john-letter'],threads:['inheritance','love-equality'],motifs:['documents']}),
 E(25,'Jane Dreams of a Ruined Thornfield','During Rochester’s absence, Jane dreams of separation, a child she cannot carry, and the house reduced to ruin.','orchard',S(['jane','Reads repeated dreams as warnings that happiness rests on unstable ground.']),day(1810,7,14,23),4,{threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['visions','weather']}),
 E(25,'A Visitor Tears the Veil','Jane wakes to see an unknown woman examine and rend the wedding veil before the mirror.','third-floor',S(['jane','Recognizes that the visitor is not Grace and demands that Rochester treat the danger as real.'],['bertha','Enters Jane’s room, destroys the bridal symbol, and returns upstairs before the household wakes.'],['rochester','Again attributes the incident to Grace and urges Jane to sleep near Adèle.']),day(1810,7,15,2),5,{items:['veil'],threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['portraits','rooms']}),
 E(26,'The Wedding Is Interrupted','Briggs and Mason stop the ceremony with proof that Rochester has a living wife.','thornfield-church',S(['jane','Hears her expected identity as bride become legally impossible in public.'],['rochester','Abandons denial and takes the witnesses to see the fact he tried to exclude.'],['mason','Confirms that his sister Bertha is Rochester’s wife and still lives.'],['briggs','Presents the legal record on behalf of Jane’s uncle.']),day(1810,7,16,9),5,{items:['john-letter'],threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['documents','thresholds']}),
 E(26,'Bertha Is Revealed','The party enters the attic and sees Rochester’s confined wife.','attic',S(['jane','Understands the hidden laughter, fire, attack, and torn veil at once.'],['rochester','Displays Bertha as explanation and asks the witnesses to compare her with Jane.'],['bertha','Confronts Rochester violently in the room where she has been confined.'],['mason','Faces his sister while remaining protected by the legal testimony he brought.'],['grace','Manages the immediate danger as the household’s paid keeper.']),day(1810,7,16,10),5,{items:['third-floor-key'],threads:['secret','confinement'],motifs:['rooms','watching']}),
 E(27,'Rochester Tells His History','Rochester recounts his arranged marriage, Caribbean life, and years of concealment.','thornfield-drawing',S(['jane','Listens with compassion while distinguishing explanation from permission to violate her conscience.'],['rochester','Offers a self-justifying but anguished account and asks Jane to build a new life outside English law.']),day(1810,7,16,15),5,{threads:['secret','love-equality','confinement'],motifs:['voices']}),
 E(27,'Jane Leaves Before Dawn','Jane refuses to become Rochester’s mistress and departs with little money while the household sleeps.','thornfield-gate',S(['jane','Chooses moral and economic uncertainty over a love that would require self-betrayal.'],['rochester','Is left behind after persuasion, grief, and authority fail to change Jane’s decision.']),day(1810,7,17,5),5,{threads:['freedom','love-equality'],motifs:['thresholds','birds']}),
 E(28,'The Journey Reaches the Midland Moors','After spending nearly all her money on travel, Jane enters an unknown upland district with no planned destination.','moors-gate',S(['jane','Arrives in a region where nobody knows her name and survival will depend on asking for help.']),day(1810,7,19,16),3,{threads:['freedom','class-work'],motifs:['weather','thresholds']}),
 E(28,'The Coach Leaves Jane at Whitcross','The coach sets Jane down at a lonely crossroads with almost no money and no known refuge.','whitcross',S(['jane','Watches her last secure transport depart and takes stock of the road, moor, and immediate need for shelter.']),day(1810,7,19,17),4,{threads:['freedom','class-work'],motifs:['weather','thresholds']}),
 E(28,'Jane Wanders Hungry on the Moor','Repeated refusals leave Jane exposed to rain and starvation until light guides her toward Moor House.','open-moor',S(['jane','Reaches physical collapse while still resisting theft and searching for a morally possible refuge.']),day(1810,7,21,21),5,{threads:['belonging','class-work'],motifs:['food','weather']}),
 E(29,'The Rivers Household Admits Jane','St John brings the exhausted stranger inside after Hannah initially turns her away.','moor-house',S(['jane','Accepts rescue without surrendering the privacy of the history she has fled.'],['st-john','Overrides suspicion because immediate duty requires shelter and medical care.'],['diana','Responds to Jane with warmth and intellectual curiosity.'],['mary','Shares nursing and household attention during Jane’s recovery.'],['hannah','Revises her first judgment when the stranger’s condition becomes unmistakable.']),day(1810,7,21,22),4,{threads:['belonging','faith'],motifs:['food','thresholds']}),
 E(29,'Jane Elliott Recovers','Jane gives an assumed surname and gradually joins the sisters’ reading and conversation.','moor-house',S(['jane','Protects her past while discovering companionship based on mind and mutual work.'],['diana','Treats the guest as a potential equal rather than a dependent.'],['mary','Builds trust through quiet shared study.'],['st-john','Observes Jane’s reserve and searches for a useful future for her.']),day(1810,8,1,15),2,{threads:['belonging','education'],motifs:['books','voices']}),
 E(30,'St John Offers the Morton School','A modest village teaching post gives Jane work and a cottage of her own.','morton-school',S(['jane','Accepts reduced social status because the work preserves independence and conscience.'],['st-john','Finds a practical place for Jane within his parish discipline.']),day(1810,8,10,12),2,{threads:['class-work','freedom'],motifs:['thresholds']}),
 E(30,'Diana and Mary Depart','The sisters return to governess positions, leaving Jane and St John to their separate duties.','moor-house',S(['jane','Parts from new friends with genuine grief but keeps the means to support herself.'],['diana','Returns reluctantly to paid work while promising continued correspondence.'],['mary','Leaves the restored household intimacy for another term of dependence.']),day(1810,8,15,9),2,{threads:['belonging','class-work'],motifs:['thresholds','documents']}),
 E(31,'Jane Faces Her First Pupils','The village school begins with limited resources and pupils whose abilities Jane initially underestimates.','morton-school',S(['jane','Feels the loss of Thornfield’s cultivated life, then rebukes herself for despising honest work.'],['st-john','Inspects the new arrangement with approval of duty rather than emotional encouragement.']),day(1810,8,20,9),2,{threads:['education','class-work'],motifs:['books']}),
 E(31,'Rosamond Visits the School','The patron’s daughter brings beauty, generosity, and visible emotional disturbance to St John’s austere routine.','morton-school',S(['jane','Quickly perceives an attraction that neither visitor nor clergyman can conceal.'],['rosamond','Shows easy kindness to the pupils and open pleasure in St John’s presence.'],['st-john','Responds intensely to Rosamond, then restores the self-command required by his chosen mission.']),day(1810,8,20,14),3,{threads:['faith','class-work'],motifs:['watching']}),
 E(32,'The School Becomes a Community','Jane’s pupils progress, and village respect replaces her first sense of degradation.','morton-school',S(['jane','Finds dignity in specific students, useful teaching, and affection earned by daily attention.']),day(1810,10,1,10),2,{threads:['education','class-work'],motifs:['books']}),
 E(32,'Jane Draws Rosamond','Rosamond sits for a portrait while St John studies the likeness he refuses to claim in life.','morton-school',S(['jane','Uses the portrait to test whether St John will acknowledge the happiness he is rejecting.'],['rosamond','Offers her likeness freely and hopes it can bridge St John’s reserve.'],['st-john','Allows himself to look, then subordinates desire to the hardships he imagines in India.']),day(1810,10,8,16),3,{items:['drawings'],threads:['faith','love-equality'],motifs:['portraits','watching']}),
 E(33,'St John Finds Jane’s True Name','A torn scrap of paper connects Jane Elliott with the heiress sought by Briggs.','morton-school',S(['jane','Learns that anonymity has ended and demands the whole explanation rather than accepting partial control.'],['st-john','Uses the signature to confirm Jane’s identity before revealing inheritance and kinship.']),day(1810,11,5,18),4,{items:['signature'],threads:['inheritance','belonging'],motifs:['documents']}),
 E(33,'Jane Discovers Her Cousins','John Eyre’s fortune belongs to Jane, and the Rivers siblings are revealed as her relatives.','moor-house',S(['jane','Values the discovery of living family above the unexpected wealth and immediately imagines sharing both.'],['st-john','Explains the family connection with more restraint than Jane can understand.'],['diana','Becomes Jane’s cousin in fact as well as a friend in affection.'],['mary','Shares the same recovery of kinship and future independence.']),day(1810,11,5,20),4,{items:['john-letter'],threads:['inheritance','belonging'],motifs:['documents','voices']}),
 E(34,'Jane Divides the Inheritance','Jane insists that the fortune be shared equally among all four cousins.','moor-house',S(['jane','Uses money to establish equality and a permanent family rather than solitary elevation.'],['st-john','Resists the impractical generosity, then accepts Jane’s decision as legally and morally deliberate.'],['diana','Returns to Moor House freed from dependence by Jane’s division.'],['mary','Shares in rebuilding a home whose resources no longer require separation.']),day(1810,12,1,14),3,{threads:['inheritance','belonging','equality'],motifs:['documents','food']}),
 E(34,'Christmas Restores Moor House','The cousins furnish, cook, read, and celebrate together while St John remains emotionally apart.','moor-house',S(['jane','Enjoys domestic labour because it expresses chosen kinship rather than servitude.'],['diana','Fills the house with study, humour, and plans for an independent future.'],['mary','Shares the practical work and settled pleasure of homecoming.'],['st-john','Participates dutifully while orienting his real attention toward India.']),day(1810,12,25,18),2,{threads:['belonging','faith'],motifs:['food','fire-ice']}),
 E(35,'St John Proposes Marriage for India','St John argues that Jane’s abilities make her a suitable missionary wife, though he does not love her.','moor-house',S(['jane','Offers service as a sister but refuses a marriage that would erase emotional truth and personal freedom.'],['st-john','Treats vocation, fitness, and religious authority as sufficient grounds for an irrevocable union.']),day(1811,5,5,20),5,{threads:['faith','equality','freedom'],motifs:['voices','confinement']}),
 E(35,'Jane Hears Rochester Call','At the brink of submission, Jane hears Rochester’s voice call her name across an impossible distance.','open-moor',S(['jane','Breaks from St John’s pressure and decides to seek factual knowledge of Rochester’s condition.'],['st-john','Finds his influence abruptly displaced by an experience he cannot direct.']),day(1811,5,7,23),5,{mentioned:['rochester'],threads:['love-equality','faith'],motifs:['voices','visions']}),
 E(36,'Jane Finds Thornfield in Ruins','Jane returns and discovers the house roofless, blackened, and abandoned.','thornfield-gate',S(['jane','Confronts the material fulfilment of her old dreams before knowing who survived.']),day(1811,5,10,15),5,{threads:['secret','love-equality'],motifs:['fire-ice','visions']}),
 E(36,'The Fire’s Outcome Is Recounted','At an inn Jane learns that Bertha burned the house and died, while Rochester lost a hand and his sight rescuing others.','battlements',S(['jane','Receives the hidden household’s conclusion as history and immediately asks where Rochester lives.'],['rochester','Is described as having saved servants and attempted to reach Bertha before the roof fell.'],['bertha','Dies after escaping to the battlements during the fire she set.']),day(1811,5,10,16),5,{threads:['secret','love-equality','confinement'],motifs:['fire-ice','voices'],flashback:true}),
 E(37,'Jane Finds Rochester at Ferndean','Jane enters the secluded house and lets Rochester recognize her by voice and touch.','ferndean',S(['jane','Returns independently, financially secure and free to choose the relationship she once had to flee.'],['rochester','Moves from disbelief and fear of abandonment toward accepting Jane’s real presence.']),day(1811,5,11,18),5,{threads:['love-equality','belonging'],motifs:['voices','watching']}),
 E(37,'They Meet on New Terms','Jane tells enough of her inheritance and family to establish that dependence no longer structures the proposal.','ferndean',S(['jane','Offers marriage as an autonomous equal who can care without surrendering herself.'],['rochester','Accepts help and love without the wealth, household mastery, or concealment that shaped Thornfield.']),day(1811,5,12,12),4,{threads:['love-equality','equality'],motifs:['watching','birds']}),
 E(38,'Jane and Rochester Marry','A quiet marriage begins the shared domestic life Jane narrates from ten years’ distance.','ferndean',S(['jane','Marries by her own decision and joins intimacy with retained voice, property, and family connection.'],['rochester','Enters marriage after confession, loss, and reunion have removed the earlier structure of deception.']),day(1811,5,15,11),4,{threads:['love-equality','belonging','equality'],motifs:['thresholds']}),
 E(38,'Ten Years Later','Jane records their son, Rochester’s partial recovery of sight, her cousins’ lives, and St John’s final letter from India.','ferndean',S(['jane','Looks back from a durable marriage while preserving active ties to Diana, Mary, Adèle, and St John.'],['rochester','Shares parenthood and has recovered enough sight to see his firstborn son.'],['adele','Has grown under healthier schooling and Jane’s continued affectionate guidance.'],['st-john','Writes from India with undiminished certainty that his work and approaching death fulfil his calling.']),day(1821,5,15,14),3,{items:['st-john-letter'],threads:['love-equality','belonging','faith'],motifs:['documents','watching']})
